```cpp 
TazGraph/Src/AssetManager/PythonEngineCommands.cpp 
```
If you need to add function related to control of simdump simulation go to: 
```cpp 
TazGraphEngine/src/DataManager/DataManager.h 
```

#Save/Load Python state
Using python, we can also save the state of envirnoment in .pkl format by executing:
```cpp

import pickle

def my_object():
    return 4;


with open("state.pkl", "wb") as f:
    pickle.dump(my_object, f)


```

To load, do:
```cpp

with open("state.pkl", "rb") as f:
    my_object = pickle.load(f)

print(my_object());

```
*/
